- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'No'` on `b1 -> n3` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v1 = 'Yes'` on `b1 -> n4` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v2 = 'No'` on `b2 -> n6` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | Guard `v2 = 'Yes'` on `b2 -> n7` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n3,"v1 = 'No'"); guard(b1,n4,"v1 = 'Yes'"); guard(b2,n6,"v2 = 'No'"); guard(b2,n7,"v2 = 'Yes'")
- [L2] LSC2 failed: Guards outgoing from an XOR branch must be mutually exclusive. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Branch `b2` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range.
- [L3] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Branch `b2` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range.
